    <tags>bff, ai, content-understanding, package</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add IInvoiceAi.ReadInvoiceAsync backed by an internal Content Understanding client (REST over IHttpClientFactory, preview API 2026-06-01-preview primary with a GA 2025-11-01 fallback analyzer per D-81, managed identity) that calls the custom analyzer sprk_invoice_vN once and maps header, fee lines, expense lines and timekeeper summary — every field with confidence, page and bounding box — to a typed result, with stable reason codes for unreadable documents. If task 005 was no-go, STOP before coding (see escalation).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Azure AI SDKs, managed identity in the BFF, and the PublicContracts AI facades. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>IInvoiceAi.ReadInvoiceAsync returns a typed extracted invoice or throws a typed exception with reason code; the client lives internal under Services/Ai; options bind the ContentUnderstanding section from task 003; a health check reports a missing analyzer with a stable code; the package's publish-size delta is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec Processing Pipeline step 1 and FR-21: one analyze call to the custom analyzer (D-49); fields with confidence and page / bounding box feed the line's extraction-confidence JSON (FR-04). Spike results and the go / no-go are in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/extraction-spike.md (task 005); the analyzer JSON is task 004's (infrastructure/content-understanding/sprk-invoice-v1.json); the config section ContentUnderstanding (Endpoint, ApiVersion, AnalyzerId) is added to appsettings.template.json by task 003. Research: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/research/content-understanding-vs-docintel.md (bundled PDFs: contentCategories / enableSegment routing, page-number questions at :436). Fallback if no-go: DI prebuilt-layout via Services/Ai/DocumentIntelligenceService.cs:147 ParseDocumentLayoutAsync plus an extraction Action, behind the same method.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (one PackageReference with Version — central package management is off; see Azure.AI.DocumentIntelligence at :117)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAi.cs, NullInvoiceAi.cs, InvoiceAiContracts.cs (ReadInvoiceAsync + extracted-invoice DTOs)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/ContentUnderstanding/ (internal client, result mapper, health check)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/ContentUnderstandingOptions.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AnalysisServicesModule.cs (InvoiceAi registered at :1402, NullInvoiceAi at :588 — register the client beside them)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/TextExtractorService.cs:103-128 (CreateDocIntelClient: endpoint + DI TokenCredential)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AiModule.cs:116-136 (DI TokenCredential use)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/SignalsModule.cs:123-139 and Services/Signals/SignalEvaluatorHealthCheck.cs (health-check registration)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/ContentUnderstanding/ (mapper and failure tests from scrubbed JSON fixtures)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="required">Reshaped IInvoiceAi and InvoiceAiContracts.cs.</dependency>
      <dependency task="005" status="required">Go / no-go, chosen arm and API version, measured package delta, field names actually returned.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-81 (owner, 2026-10-15)">Path-A exception: the analyzer built on `2026-06-01-preview` is primary; a GA fallback analyzer on `2025-11-01` with the same field schema is kept in step and selected by configuration only (`ContentUnderstanding:ApiVersion`, `ContentUnderstanding:AnalyzerId`; no code change to switch). Preview and GA analyzers do not interoperate, so each is deployed on its own API version by scripts/content-understanding/Deploy-Analyzers.ps1 (extend it to accept the preview API version and a preview definition file under infrastructure/content-understanding/, keeping its idempotent create / no-change / refuse-without--Replace behaviour; the 004 "no preview string" criterion is superseded by D-81). The GA SDK Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding 1.1.0 does not cover the preview API: implement the client as a thin REST client over IHttpClientFactory with a managed-identity token (DefaultAzureCredential, scope https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/.default), serving both API versions; do not add a prerelease SDK. Add the 1.1.0 package only if a concrete need appears, and then report it as an escalation (BFF hygiene, NFR-12). Carry the spike conditions: deterministic completion step (hh:mm hours, missing rates), analyzer v2 wording for hours and non-US dates, page-range analysis of very long PDFs, and field names as actually returned (notes/extraction-spike.md). Cite the D-81 path-A exception in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; this task's package must be justified in the PR with its measured delta.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-12 / D-50">Exactly one new package: Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding 1.1.0. No other NuGet or npm package; no raw REST client written instead of the SDK unless 005 recorded that the SDK cannot do a required call (then escalate).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-47 / ADR-028">Managed identity only (the DI TokenCredential); no key option, no key in config. Endpoint, API version and analyzer id come from ContentUnderstandingOptions using exactly task 003's key names.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">The SDK client is internal to Services/Ai and reachable only through IInvoiceAi.ReadInvoiceAsync; Finance code never references Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding types. The extracted-invoice DTOs live in PublicContracts.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-21">A document the analyzer cannot read raises a typed exception with a stable reason code: invoice.read.unreadable (encrypted / corrupt), invoice.read.page_limit (over the configured page limit), invoice.read.no_invoice (no invoice found), invoice.read.service_failed (transient / service error, retryable). Never return a partial result as success. Non-USD currency is returned as read — the finding is the evaluator's, not a failure here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015 / NFR-11">Logs carry document id, page count, timings and reason codes only — never field values or narratives.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">NullInvoiceAi.ReadInvoiceAsync throws FeatureDisabledException ai.invoice.disabled like its other methods.</constraint>
  </constraints>

