  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor FULL. Read notes/extraction-spike.md. If the decision is no-go or the file is missing, STOP (escalation). Record the chosen arm and API version.</step>
    <step order="1">Use the researcher agent (root CLAUDE.md §15) to confirm the 1.1.0 SDK surface for analyze, result fields, confidence, source / bounding box and the long-running operation; record findings in notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the extracted-invoice DTOs in InvoiceAiContracts.cs: header fields per FR-21; lines (date, timekeeper as billed, title as billed, hours, rate, amount, narrative, codes as billed, line type Fee / Expense); timekeeper summary rows; each field value carries confidence (0-1), page (1-based, original-file numbering) and bounding box {page, x, y, w, h} normalised 0-1, so 049 can write FR-04's extraction-confidence JSON directly.</step>
    <step order="3">Add ContentUnderstandingOptions (section ContentUnderstanding, keys from 003, MaxPages default 300) with ValidateOnStart that requires a well-formed Endpoint only when one is set.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the internal client and mapper; one analyze call per document; never enable input truncation (a document over MaxPages is refused with invoice.read.page_limit, not silently cut); map analyzer failures and empty results to the reason codes; add ReadInvoiceAsync to IInvoiceAi / InvoiceAi / NullInvoiceAi.</step>
    <step order="5">Add a health check: endpoint configured and analyzer missing or unreachable reports Unhealthy with description code content_understanding.analyzer_missing; endpoint not configured reports Healthy with a description saying the reader is not configured.</step>
    <step order="6">Unit tests from scrubbed analyzer-result JSON fixtures (from the spike, no PII): full mapping, missing optional fields, multi-page bounding boxes, each reason code, Null peer. Add one live test that reports Skipped when the endpoint env var is absent (see the Skipped convention in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests.csproj:26).</step>
    <step order="7">Build, test; measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build and compare with 005's figure.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations (DTO choices 049 depends on, measured delta) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If notes/extraction-spike.md records no-go for Content Understanding, or has no decision, STOP and present the fallback (DI prebuilt-layout via DocumentIntelligenceService plus an extraction Action, same ReadInvoiceAsync contract) for owner confirmation before writing code.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the measured publish-size delta of the package is 5 MB or more, STOP and present it (root CLAUDE.md §10 threshold) before merging.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the SDK cannot authenticate with the DI TokenCredential or lacks a call the spike relied on, STOP — do not add a key or a hand-written REST client without owner approval.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>DocumentIntelligenceService.ParseDocumentLayoutAsync (:147) returns layout text without invoice semantics; InvoiceAnalysisService.ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync uses text + LLM. Nothing references Content Understanding today (grep -i ContentUnderstanding in src finds nothing).</existing>
    <extension>DocumentIntelligenceService wraps a different SDK and API (prebuilt-layout); the analyzer result model (fields with confidence and source) has no equivalent there. The method extends IInvoiceAi instead of adding a facade; ContentUnderstandingOptions is new because DocumentIntelligenceOptions is the OpenAI / DI config and its key-based DocIntel settings must not apply here.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-21 and NFR-04 fail: no per-field confidence or page / bounding box, so the rejection rule (FR-26) cannot tell reliable from unreliable reads and reviewers cannot see where a value came from.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test ; dotnet publish (size measurement)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj, Services/Ai/ContentUnderstanding/*, Configuration/ContentUnderstandingOptions.cs, PublicContracts IInvoiceAi / InvoiceAi / NullInvoiceAi / InvoiceAiContracts.cs, AnalysisServicesModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/ContentUnderstanding/*</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per D-81, switching ContentUnderstanding:ApiVersion / AnalyzerId between the preview primary and the GA fallback needs no code change: a test runs ReadInvoiceAsync against each configuration (seam test with recorded responses), and both analyzers are deployed in dev by Deploy-Analyzers.ps1 with a second run reporting no change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No prerelease package is referenced; if Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding is not needed, the publish-size delta for the client is reported as code-only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a scrubbed analyzer result fixture, ReadInvoiceAsync maps every FR-21 header field and every fee, expense and timekeeper-summary row, each with confidence, page and normalised bounding box.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: fixtures or stubs for encrypted, over-page-limit, no-invoice and service-error results raise the typed exception with invoice.read.unreadable, invoice.read.page_limit, invoice.read.no_invoice and invoice.read.service_failed respectively; none returns a partial result.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A non-USD currency value maps through unchanged and does not throw.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NullInvoiceAi.ReadInvoiceAsync throws FeatureDisabledException with ErrorCode ai.invoice.disabled.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The client is constructed with the DI TokenCredential; ContentUnderstandingOptions has no key property; grep finds no Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding using outside Services/Ai.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The health check reports Unhealthy with content_understanding.analyzer_missing when the analyzer lookup fails, and Healthy with a not-configured description when Endpoint is empty; the host starts in both cases.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj gains exactly one PackageReference (Azure.AI.ContentUnderstanding 1.1.0); no other package changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The live test reports Skipped (not Passed) when no endpoint is configured.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-21, FR-47, NFR-11, NFR-12, D-49, D-50, D-53. The brief calls this the only new package. Bundled PDFs: follow the routing approach 005 chose (research note §"classify, segment, and analyze"); if 005 left that open, take the single-call routed form and record it. Shared append point: appsettings*.json (only if this task must add MaxPages beside 003's keys).

    COMPLETED 2026-10-15 (FULL rigor). As built: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/043-cu-client.md.
    - D-81 (path-A exception, spec.md ADR Tensions): preview 2026-06-01-preview + sprk_invoice_v2p primary, GA 2025-11-01 + sprk_invoice_v2 fallback, switched by ContentUnderstanding:ApiVersion + AnalyzerId only; seam tests run both; ArchTest keeps the two analyzer files in step.
    - Supersedes the "exactly one PackageReference" criterion: NO package added (thin REST client over IHttpClientFactory + DI TokenCredential; no prerelease SDK). The csproj is unchanged; the publish-size delta is code-only (notes, BFF hygiene).
    - Bundles: no router (spike section 7). Long documents: page ranges of PageRangeSize (default 20). Completion ports the spike complete() plus a day/month post-check.
    - Both analyzers deployed on dev by Deploy-Analyzers.ps1; second run NO CHANGE. Spike-only analyzers deleted.
    - Tests at KEEP paths (seam / domain / contract / ArchTests), not the POML's Services/Ai path. Code-review, adr-check and one adversarial pass done; all seven adversarial findings resolved (notes, Review findings).
    - Not done here: setting ContentUnderstanding__Endpoint on spaarke-bff-dev (deploy work); TASK-INDEX (main session).</notes>

